{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they shall take of the blood and put it.</b> By dipping a bunch of hyssop, as Moshe explained to Israel; and what this passage made brief, a second passage explained." "<b>On the two doorposts.</b> On both sides of the entrance." "<b>And on the lintel.</b> From the root וישקף — it is the crossbeam of the entrance seen above. And all this — lest they all be able to come in at the time of slaughter; now they will all see the blood. Their fear is placed there for disgrace. Another interpretation: so that the blood be in the shape of a letter <b>chet</b> to protect the entrance, so that the destroyer not be given entry into it, and it is a sign of life." "<b>On the houses.</b> In the houses — a model of 'by their armies' — 'by your sword you shall live.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:06.702795080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}